Strategy: // CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// Analysis of current situation:
// - Best result: attempt 12 at 14% accuracy, 100% syntax (7/50 unique valid molecules)
// - Attempt 18 (previous): same accuracy 14% but syntax dropped to 80% due to temperature=1.8 in R-group
//   The failing examples all output "C=CC(=O)OC1CCCCC2CCCCC>>" - unclosed ring, invalid SMILES
//
// Key observations:
// 1. The 10 syntax failures all produce "C=CC(=O)OC1CCCCC2CCCCC" - a bicyclic ring attempt that never closes
// 2. This happens because temperature=1.8 in R-group encourages ring openings ("1","2") but the budget
//    runs out before the rings close
// 3. The fix: stay with temperature=1.6 for R-group (attempt 12 had 100% syntax with this)
//    BUT we need to improve DIVERSITY to go from 7/50 to 17+/50 unique molecules
//
// Root cause of low diversity (7/50 unique): The model converges to the same scaffold and R-group.
// With SafeSoftConstrainedStep(8.0) for scaffold + SafeTemperatureConstrainedStep(1.6) for R-group,
// we get 14% accuracy but only 7 unique molecules.
//
// Why 7 unique? The model generates the same 7-8 molecules repeatedly across 50 rollouts.
// Each rollout should be independent sampling, but the distribution is too peaked.
//
// Strategy to improve diversity while maintaining syntax:
// 1. DON'T use temperature=1.8 (caused syntax failures)
// 2. EXTEND the scaffold phase to only 4 tokens (not 6) so the model has more freedom earlier
//    The scaffold "C=CC(=O)O" is about 6 tokens, so using soft step for only 4 forces the model
//    to commit to the acrylate pattern but allows more variation in the ester oxygen step
// 3. Use ConfidenceGatedStep for ENTIRE R-group generation
//    ConfidenceGatedStep returns the top free LM token if it's parser-valid, hard-masks otherwise
//    This gives the MOST natural/diverse distribution while maintaining validity
// 4. Increase minLength to 15 to force longer R-groups (more structural diversity)
// 5. Better guidance that emphasizes diverse UNCOMMON acrylates
//
// Actually let me reconsider. Attempt 12 used:
// - SafeSoftConstrainedStep for first 6 tokens
// - SafeTemperatureConstrainedStep(1.6) for R-group
// - minLength=12
// - Result: 14% accuracy, 100% syntax, 7/50 unique
//
// The 10 syntax failures in attempt 18 are from temperature=1.8 producing unclosed ring SMILES.
// Going BACK to temperature=1.6 with the exact attempt 12 setup would give us the same 7/50.
//
// To genuinely improve diversity I need a different approach:
//
// INSIGHT: The failure mode in attempt 18 is that temperature=1.8 opens rings that never close.
// But the diversity comes from WHICH R-group is chosen in the first 2-3 R-group tokens.
// If those tokens are "OC" vs "CC" vs "1C" vs "NC", we get very different molecules.
//
// APPROACH: Use ConfidenceGatedStep for R-group. This uses the free LM distribution when
// the top token is already parser-valid. The free LM is sampled with the model's own temperature
// (which may be 1.0 or whatever the inference server uses). This gives more natural diversity
// than forcing a specific temperature scaling.
//
// Also CRITICAL: the failing rollouts all produce the same molecule "C=CC(=O)OC1CCCCC2CCCCC".
// This is the cyclohexyl/bicyclic pattern. The guidance has "C=CC(=O)OC1CCCCC1" as a prompt example,
// which is cyclohexyl acrylate. The model is fixating on this because we show it as an example.
// REMOVE cyclohexyl acrylate from the guidance examples! Or at least put it far down the list.
//
// Also: Don't use ring closures in examples (no "1" or "2" digits) to steer away from ring patterns.
// Linear alkyl and heteroatom R-groups are safer for syntax.
//
// REVISED PLAN:
// 1. Guidance with ONLY linear and branched alkyl/heteroatom acrylates (NO ring examples)
// 2. Scaffold phase (< 6 tokens): SafeSoftConstrainedStep(8.0) - same as attempt 12
// 3. R-group phase (6-20 tokens): ConfidenceGatedStep - uses free LM when valid, hard mask otherwise
// 4. Late phase (> 20 tokens): SafeTemperatureConstrainedStep(1.4) to wrap up gracefully
// 5. minLength=14 (slightly longer than attempt 12's 12 to force more diverse R-groups)
// 6. Close when complete and minLength satisfied
//
// This should:
// - Maintain 100% syntax (no ring-opening temperature issues)
// - Improve diversity through ConfidenceGatedStep's natural LM distribution
// - Force longer, more diverse R-groups through minLength=14
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// parser_validity (insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)):
//   - Initialization: holds by preconditions (insideConstrained ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrained)).
//   - OpenConstrainedSpan: sets currentConstrainedOut := [] and insideConstrainedOut := true.
//     parser.IsValidPrefix([]) holds by the method's requires clause. Invariant preserved.
//   - CloseConstrainedSpan branch: sets insideConstrainedOut := false, making the implication
//     vacuously true; also sets currentConstrainedOut := []. Invariant preserved.
//   - SafeSoftConstrainedStep path (scaffold): returns next where next == eosToken OR
//     parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut + [next]). On non-EOS, AppendConstrainedToken
//     sets currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrainedOut + [next], which is parser-valid by postcondition.
//   - ConfidenceGatedStep path (R-group): returns next where next == eosToken OR
//     parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut + [next]) (by ConfidenceGatedStep postcondition -
//     it either returns a valid LM token or falls back to hard-masked valid token). AppendConstrainedToken
//     preserves parser validity.
//   - SafeTemperatureConstrainedStep path (late): hard-masks to valid tokens plus EOS.
//     AppendConstrainedToken preserves parser validity by contract.
//   - EOS path: insideConstrainedOut unchanged, currentConstrainedOut unchanged; invariant preserved.
//
// progress (|generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps):
//   - OpenConstrainedSpan: steps += 1, generated grows by 1 token ("<<").
//     Before: |gen| <= |genPfx| + s. After: |gen|+1 <= |genPfx| + (s+1). Preserved.
//   - CloseConstrainedSpan: steps += 1, generated grows by 1 token (">>"). Same analysis. Preserved.
//   - SafeSoftConstrainedStep step: steps += 1. Non-EOS path: AppendConstrainedToken appends 1 token.
//     |gen|+1 <= |genPfx| + (steps+1). EOS path: steps += 1, no append. Both preserved.
//   - ConfidenceGatedStep step: steps += 1. Non-EOS path: AppendConstrainedToken appends 1 token. Preserved.
//   - SafeTemperatureConstrainedStep step: same as above. Preserved.
//   - All branches: |generated| grows by at most 1 while steps grows by exactly 1. Invariant holds.
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END
generated := generatedPrefix;
insideConstrainedOut := insideConstrained;
currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained;
cost := 0;

var guidance: string := "Task: output exactly ONE valid SMILES string for a molecule in the ACRYLATE class. Acrylate core scaffold: C=CC(=O)O- (acrylic ester) or C=C(C)C(=O)O- (methacrylic ester). Generate diverse acrylates with linear or branched alkyl or heteroatom R-groups. Examples of valid acrylates: C=CC(=O)OCCO, C=CC(=O)OCCCO, C=CC(=O)OCCCCO, C=CC(=O)OCCCCC, C=CC(=O)OCCCCCC, C=CC(=O)OCCCCCCC, C=CC(=O)OCCCCCCCC, C=C(C)C(=O)OCCC, C=C(C)C(=O)OCCCC, C=C(C)C(=O)OCCCCC, C=C(C)C(=O)OCCO, C=C(C)C(=O)OCCCO, C=CC(=O)OCC(C)C, C=CC(=O)OC(C)(C)C, C=CC(=O)OCCC(C)C, C=CC(=O)OCC(C)(C)C, C=CC(=O)OCC(CC)CC, C=CC(=O)OCCOCCO, C=CC(=O)OCC(O)CO, C=CC(=O)OCCN, C=CC(=O)OCCCN, C=CC(=O)OCCOCCOC, C=CC(=O)OCCC(C)(C)C, C=C(C)C(=O)OCC(C)C, C=C(C)C(=O)OC(C)(C)C, C=C(C)C(=O)OCCC(C)C, C=CC(=O)OCCCCCCCCC, C=CC(=O)OCCCCCCCCCC, C=C(C)C(=O)OCCCCCCC, C=CC(=O)OCCOCCOCCO. Output the SMILES string and NOTHING else.";
helpers.AppendTaskGuidance(lm, guidance);

var steps: nat := 0;
var minLength: nat := 14;

// Open a constrained span immediately if not already inside one
if !insideConstrainedOut && steps < maxSteps {
  var og, oi, oc := helpers.OpenConstrainedSpan(lm, generated);
  generated := og;
  insideConstrainedOut := oi;
  currentConstrainedOut := oc;
  steps := steps + 1;
}

while steps + 1 < maxSteps
  invariant 0 <= steps <= maxSteps
  invariant lm.ValidTokensIdsLogits()
  invariant !insideConstrainedOut ==> currentConstrainedOut == []
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
  invariant insideConstrainedOut ==> |currentConstrainedOut| <= |generated|
  invariant |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
  decreases maxSteps - steps
{
  if !insideConstrainedOut {
    break;
  } else if parser.IsCompletePrefix(currentConstrainedOut) && |currentConstrainedOut| >= minLength {
    // Reserve 1 step for close
    var cg, ci, cc := helpers.CloseConstrainedSpan(lm, parser, generated, currentConstrainedOut);
    generated := cg;
    insideConstrainedOut := ci;
    currentConstrainedOut := cc;
    steps := steps + 1;
    break;
  } else {
    var constrainedPrompt := prompt + generated[..|generated| - |currentConstrainedOut|];
    var spanLen := |currentConstrainedOut|;
    var next: Token;
    if spanLen < 6 {
      // Scaffold phase: use soft constrained step to guide toward acrylate scaffold
      var nextSoft, softOk := helpers.SafeSoftConstrainedStep(
        lm, parser, constrainedPrompt, currentConstrainedOut, 8.0, eosToken
      );
      next := nextSoft;
    } else if spanLen < 22 {
      // R-group phase: use confidence-gated step for natural LM diversity
      var nextCG, wasCG := helpers.ConfidenceGatedStep(
        lm, parser, constrainedPrompt, currentConstrainedOut, eosToken
      );
      next := nextCG;
    } else {
      // Late phase: moderate temperature to wrap up
      next := helpers.SafeTemperatureConstrainedStep(
        lm, parser, constrainedPrompt, currentConstrainedOut, 1.3, eosToken
      );
    }
    steps := steps + 1;
    if next == eosToken {
      if parser.IsCompletePrefix(currentConstrainedOut) && |currentConstrainedOut| >= minLength && steps < maxSteps {
        var cg, ci, cc := helpers.CloseConstrainedSpan(lm, parser, generated, currentConstrainedOut);
        generated := cg;
        insideConstrainedOut := ci;
        currentConstrainedOut := cc;
        steps := steps + 1;
      }
      break;
    } else {
      var ag, ai, ac := helpers.AppendConstrainedToken(
        lm, parser, generated, currentConstrainedOut, next
      );
      generated := ag;
      insideConstrainedOut := ai;
      currentConstrainedOut := ac;
    }
  }
}

// Final close attempt if still inside and complete
if insideConstrainedOut && parser.IsCompletePrefix(currentConstrainedOut) && |currentConstrainedOut| >= minLength && steps < maxSteps {
  var cg, ci, cc := helpers.CloseConstrainedSpan(lm, parser, generated, currentConstrainedOut);
  generated := cg;
  insideConstrainedOut := ci;
  currentConstrainedOut := cc;
  steps := steps + 1;
}

cost := steps;

